   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to blue lights on ambulances, emergency ambulance service vehicles and county emergency medical services vehicles",
    "basePrintNo": "S5483",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5483-2011",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §375, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5483\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to blue lights on\nambulances, emergency ambulance service vehicles and county emergency\nmedical services vehicles\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\nTo better protect ambulances and\nother emergency service vehicles at night by giving them the option\nto use rear projecting blue-lights.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\nSection one of the bill amends section\n375 of the Vehicle and Traffic Law to include ambulances among the\nvehicles currently given the option to utilize blue-lights.\n\nSection two contains the effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nAmbulance workers regularly attend to emergency\nincidents on the state's highways. Performing emergency duties on the\nside of the road presents significant risks to them. Unfortunately,\nin these situations, many emergency responders are killed or injured\nas a result of being struck by a passing motorist. Studies have shown\nthat the blue light is the most noticeable light, and as a result,\nprovides the highest level of safety.\n\nCurrent law allows for one or more blue lights or combination of blue,\nred and/or white lights to be affixed to a fire or police vehicle\nprovided that they are displayed for rear projection only.\n\nStudies conducted by Ford Motor Company and the Florida Highway Patrol\nclearly indicated that the perception-decision-response process in\ndriving, especially at night, favored the blue light over other\ncolors, particularly when approaching from the rear.\n\nThis bill would give the option for ambulances to be equipped with\nrear facing blue lights, extending the perceptual advantage\nattributed to them to ambulances.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nThis is a new bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone to the State.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
